WEBVTT

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:38.790
Sasshi and Arumi had vowed to each other...

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.700
...that they would get back to their own world this time.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.460
Oh, but then, but then...

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.080
The place they arrived at was Tokimeki Campus Shopping Arcade.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.870
It was a world overflowing with cuties...

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.290
...putting Sasshi's carnal desires into overdrive.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:54.210
Of course, Arumi's the one who ultimately suffers.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.780
At any rate, Arumi turned into a goblin for some reason.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.880
No matter what she did, everything backfired on her.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.280
I guess this was a world that was convenient only for Sasshi.

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.520
Finally, Arumi-chan lost it.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.690
She just left Sasshi and wandered off somewhere.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:10.190
And then, Eutus appeared.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:11.960
"Stay at my place tonight." Huh?

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:13.260
Where's your place? Is it close by?

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:14.730
How many minutes 'till we get there?!

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.360
Aren't we there yet?

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.500
Your house is awfully far away.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.310
Oh, you've been walking?

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:31.630
What the heck is this?! A moving walkway?!

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:35.010
People from Osaka always choose to walk, they can't help it.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.020
This is not a moving walkway.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:38.790
Here, regardless of whether you walk or run...

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.780
...the distance you traverse won't count.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:44.990
We are currently traveling through a locus between karmic bodies...

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:47.090
...whose fates are linked.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.600
In this place, you can jump in any direction...

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.730
...above the first seven dimensions, which includes time.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:54.670
Did you get that?

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.940
Mister, I hate to say this...

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:02.820
I'm pretty far down on the stupid end, even for a grade school kid.

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:04.610
I'd forgotten.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.680
In other words, no matter how far we go in space-time...

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.250
...the location will always remain Abeno.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:11.790
Oh, I know about that.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.250
We've jumped to so many different places, I'm practically sick of it.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:18.220
Does that mean we're going to another weird shopping arcade?

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:23.360
In that case, take us somewhere sharp, kinda like you.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:53.460
What is this?!

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:57.160
A goblin! I've become a goblin!

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:01.860
It seems your fate is not linked to this world.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:02.800
Fate?

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:04.770
That's right, fate.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:08.130
Like saying, "It was fate" after an unexpected encounter.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.720
Also, talk of marriage is called discussion of fate.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:12.610
Oh, right.

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:14.950
The one with the Chinese character that looks a lot like "green", huh?

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:18.180
Just until the other day, I'd thought the phrase was "stinking green".

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:22.080
The world and the people in it are linked to one another by fate at all times.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:24.790
If a soul's chain of fate to that world is broken...

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:27.420
...that individual has no choice but to become a goblin.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:31.820
You are an existence that does not fundamentally belong in this world.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.840
Don't worry.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.130
You'll become human again when you go back to your own world.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.140
I'm more of a city boy.

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:43.870
I suppose maybe it's only natural that my fate's not linked to this depressing field.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:48.350
Oh, I see! That's why Arumi turned into a goblin.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:50.590
Arumi and bishoujo games have their fate linked about...

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:53.950
...as much as an old lady from Osaka and a Catholic nunnery.

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.960
Let's get going before the sun sets.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.560
We'll be traveling in three dimensions from here.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.570
What?! So, we're gonna walk in the end anyway?! What a pain.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:05.270
What the heck? If you've got a car, just say so already.

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:07.570
I'm a weak 21st century kid, ya know.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.870
Twenty-first century?

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:15.750
Whoa! It's a helicopter!

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:51.140
Hey, Mister, what's that?!

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:53.680
Come on, Mister!

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.140
Mister!

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.150
Do not look up!

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.110
It's a goblin! There's a goblin flying in the sky!

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:46.170
Hey, this wouldn't happen to be ancient Kyoto, would it?

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:49.560
Looking at it from above it had a sort of checkerboard pattern.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:53.680
I feel like maybe I'd seen it in a social studies book or something.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:54.640
Or was that Japanese class?

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.580
Good job figuring it out.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:58.480
Historically speaking, we're in the Heian Era.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:00.640
The 10th century city of Kyoto.

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:04.450
This place is not like the nonsensical shopping arcades...

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:06.650
...that sprang forth from your mind.

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:09.560
As long as you make scientifically correct jumps...

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:11.990
...you can travel to proper worlds like this one.

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:16.660
Then, you mean this is the real world?!

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:18.120
Real?

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:21.870
No, come on, hold on a second, Mr. Eutus!

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:24.600
What's a helicopter doing in the proper Heian Era?

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:28.670
That's right, you're a goblin.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:31.840
This will be the first time I've ever invited a goblin into my home.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.810
Uh, sorry about that.

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:37.930
Well, then, pardon me.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:05.170
What's such a common living room doing in the Heian Era?

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:15.420
There we go!

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:19.640
And he's a mega ordinary middle-aged guy too.

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.430
What? Oh, the bathroom's in the corner over there.

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:25.070
It's the type that spouts warm water.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:26.830
Paper's a luxury item here.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:29.000
Pitcher Takahashi throws!

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.630
Strike!

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.700
Mister, who the heck are ya?

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:37.170
I can understand that you can't buy toilet paper in the Heian Era...

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:40.140
...but then, where're ya getting this electricity from?

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:41.980
Electricity?

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:46.670
The chi of yin, the chi of yang, spiritual chi, and the 24 seasons of the year.

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:50.750
If it's about chi, that is indeed my field of specialization.

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:53.450
Mister, didn't you say you were a scientist?

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:56.590
Yes, that's right, but in this era, we're not called that.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:00.470
Here, we are called Onmyou mystics!

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:03.740
Onmyou mystics? You mean those Onmyou mystics?

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:06.240
The ones that used shikigami?

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:08.150
The ones that even the rulers of that time feared?

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:12.080
It was hugely popular among office ladies and stuff...

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:14.780
...and there was some guy who got mega famous off it...

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:16.920
Yumemakura Baku?

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:17.990
Wrong!

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:20.880
Let's see, what was it?

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:24.560
I know! It's Abe, Abe...

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:25.690
Abeno Midosuji?

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:29.250
Hey, how does a grade school kid like you know such an old song?!

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:30.830
Oh, I've got it.

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:32.030
Ashiya Douman!

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.830
Wrong! That's the bad guy!

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:37.510
The good guy! The good guy!

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:39.300
Oh, that's Abeno Seimei.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:40.720
That's right.

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:44.220
So, do you get to meet such famous people here?

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.480
I'm Abeno Seimei!

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:49.220
Okay, never mind the jokes.

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:49.980
This is not a joke!

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:53.940
What? Then you're the real Abeno Seimei-san?

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:55.260
That's right.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:56.520
Wow...

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:57.860
Aren't you a little more surprised?

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:02.230
Well, I thought it might be something like that.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:06.580
Then, what's with the non-Japanese sounding name, "Eutus"?

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:11.510
Well, I'm sort of looking to break out into the worldwide scene.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:12.970
Whoa, talk about shady.

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:18.280
That's a shikigami.

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:19.720
This thing?

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:24.520
Before, I was making full use of twelve of them for cleaning and laundry and such...

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:26.150
...but they were really loud.

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:28.590
I shut off all the other ones...

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:30.990
...and put them in storage in the shed under the bridge.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:33.070
This is awfully different from the image I had.

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:36.630
I don't know what image you're talking about, but it has nothing to do with me.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:42.530
All right! All right!

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:47.940
There's a place called Abeno Seimei Shrine...

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:50.180
...in the neighborhood of our shopping arcade.

00:10:50.180 --> 00:10:52.330
They hold a festival every summer...

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:54.910
...but does that have anything to do with you?

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:57.380
Oh, that.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:01.190
You said your name was Sasshi, right?

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:02.890
What's your last name?

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:03.850
Imamiya.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:05.390
Your family runs a bathhouse?

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:06.760
Yeah.

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:08.930
But it's been put out of business 'cause of the redevelopment...

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:10.730
...so there's no Turtle Bath anymore.

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:12.860
You sure know a lot, Mister.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:14.900
What about the girl who was with you?

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:16.360
Asahina Arumi.

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:18.400
She's from Masayuki's family, isn't she?

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:20.810
Amazing! I guess that's why you're an Onmyou mystic!

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:23.010
I had no idea you could figure out stuff like that too.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:26.370
Masayuki's Arumi's grandpa.

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:28.250
No wonder.

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:35.190
You should exist outside the karmic body over here, and yet your fate is linked to mine.

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:40.320
I've been thinking about why that might be, now I know why.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.430
What do you mean, "now I know why"?

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:44.430
You remember Mune-mune?

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:46.430
The young woman who's always chasing me around?

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:48.930
The giant-breasted girl with glasses, Mune-mune!

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.390
That's your granny, you know.

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:52.770
No way!

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:55.610
Grandma's name was Imamiya Mune...

00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:08.520
I was born into a family...

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:10.890
...that governed the entire Abeno area in the land of Settsu.

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:13.860
Since I was not in line to inherit the family estate...

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:15.830
...I traveled to Kyoto at a young age...

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:18.670
...and through an introduction on my mother's side...

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.070
...I met the Kamo family and followed the path of Onmyou mysticism.

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:25.300
Of course, while you're training, you're not allowed to visit your homeland.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:28.110
I built a reputation for myself as an Onmyou mystic...

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:30.550
...gained my independence, and came to have a house of my own.

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:32.340
It was only then that I first received permission to return home.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:36.720
It had been a full 20 years since I had last been to Abeno...

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:38.890
...and there were few people left whom I knew...

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:41.880
...but my childhood friend, Masayuki, gave me a warm welcome.

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:45.190
Masayuki had a wife.

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:47.500
Her name was Mune.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:49.700
At first, my sense of obligation towards her husband, Masayuki...

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:52.530
...led me to be the lady's confidant and I advised her on her troubles...

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:54.160
...as an Onmyou mystic, but...

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:58.430
When a man and a woman's fates are linked...

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:00.670
...no one can stop them from falling in love.

00:13:01.810 --> 00:13:03.640
As my visits to her came and went...

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.940
Mune and I eventually became very fond of each other.

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:10.140
There was a large laurel tree at their home.

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.650
I remember once when the tree was rustling in the breeze...

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:14.440
...and for some reason, we weren't able to take our eyes off it...

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:17.320
...so we both just stood there, gazing at it as if entranced.

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:20.660
Right around that time...

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:22.960
...my name was beginning to be known in the Imperial Court.

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:27.100
I was to visit the Imperial Palace for the first time...

00:13:27.100 --> 00:13:29.330
...so I had to return quickly to the capital.

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:33.270
I left without even having time to say goodbye to Mune...

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:35.240
...but when I got there, I discovered...

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:37.040
...that the stories circulating about me were all truly ridiculous.

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:40.520
Things like, I killed a frog with a leaf...

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:42.780
...or that I dueled a Buddhist priest from Harima.

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:44.880
They had absolutely nothing to do with the Onmyou way.

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:48.920
However, such legends were well received...

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:51.190
...and I was swamped with work all the time as a result.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:54.430
Matters concerning Abeno were slowly pushed aside...

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.060
...outside my field of awareness.

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:00.940
One day, on my way home...

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:03.340
...a large laurel tree caught my eye.

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:06.640
"It's rustling, even though there's no breeze..."

00:14:08.310 --> 00:14:11.570
I immediately got my things together and left for Abeno.

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:17.580
There, awaiting me, was the worst possible reality.

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:19.820
Having learned of the relationship between Mune and me...

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:21.620
Masayuki had gone mad with jealousy...

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:23.820
...and killed Mune, then killed himself.

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:25.450
He had just passed away shortly before my arrival.

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:31.070
I cradled Masayuki's still-warm body against me and I was filled with remorse.

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:32.860
I decided that I would use all the powers available to me...

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:37.060
...to bring Mune and Masayuki back into this world once again.

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:40.200
The Taizanfukun ceremony, a secret rite...

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:44.980
...was said to revive the dead.

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:50.210
It was the culmination of the Onmyou Way, the ultimate technique.

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:53.410
I had never heard of an instance where it had been successful.

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:58.250
The purpose of Onmyou techniques was to twist the upcoming realities...

00:14:58.590 --> 00:15:01.460
...thereby avoiding bad events that were expected to happen.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:04.270
This means that with each instance, you and the client...

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:07.100
...leap from the world that event is happening in...

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:10.160
...to a world where that event does not happen.

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:14.040
As long as you follow the proper and orderly linkage of fates...

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:16.840
...you cannot easily wander into nonsensical worlds.

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:20.770
But the Taizanfukun ceremony was an exception...

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:23.870
...and it fundamentally differed from those other spells.

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:27.820
Reviving the dead means nullifying what has already happened...

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:31.520
...in other words, canceling the past...

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:35.450
...and for the parties concerned to go live in a completely new world.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:41.460
This results in an enormous leap, which ignores the permutations of linked fates.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:50.210
Had the ceremony worked as it was supposed to?

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:55.540
I found myself standing alone in a strange land.

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:58.520
Trains and buses coming and going.

00:15:58.520 --> 00:15:59.920
Scenery I had never seen.

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:01.060
These buildings...

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:04.360
Abeno, one thousand years later.

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:06.230
It took me a while to comprehend.

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:10.020
In that world, Masayuki was alive.

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:12.630
And so was Mune.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:16.870
But unlike me, who had suddenly appeared...

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:19.500
...those two existed as residents of this world.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:24.480
I learned that Masayuki and Mune were not together in this world.

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:27.980
I thought that we might be able to find a better way this time.

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:33.020
I thought this might be a world where my wish would be fulfilled.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:41.860
And so, you built the Abenobashi Shopping Arcade. I see.

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:48.030
Which means, you're the reason why Arumi and I are being put through this whole mess.

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:51.360
Hey! So, what're ya gonna do about it?!

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:53.900
The reason? For what?

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:57.110
We've been dragged into these weird worlds...

00:16:57.110 --> 00:16:59.450
...and we've ended up piloting giant robots, getting chased by dinosaurs...

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.450
...and we can't go home!

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:03.520
Those weird worlds based on your geeky hobbies...

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:05.870
...seem to me like nothing more than you having fun.

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:07.350
Wrong!

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:09.020
You remember those bird and turtle signs...

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:11.030
...in the four cardinal directions of the shopping arcade?!

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:16.000
The last one of those, the pelican, fell with Masa-jii and broke!

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:18.000
And right after that, funky things started happening all over town!

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.900
I don't really get why my hobbies are the only ones that become real...

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:24.840
...but anyway, we're trapped in these neat, but annoying worlds!

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:27.310
But scientifically speaking, that's impossible!

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.650
Then what is scientifically possible?!

00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:33.980
Those statues of the four godly beasts were simply there to activate the flow of chi.

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:36.580
If they broke, the chi in the town would only go stagnant...

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:38.450
...and in fact, things would just stop happening.

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:42.860
If such an enormous leap were to happen, it's possible to think...

00:17:42.860 --> 00:17:47.120
...that an echo of the Taizanfukun ceremony I conducted there somehow took effect.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.600
See? It is your fault after all.

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:51.630
I swear! Every year, ever since I was little...

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:53.530
I've carried the portable shrine during the festival...

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:56.270
...worshipping you, "O Seimei-san, O Seimei-san."

00:17:56.270 --> 00:17:58.970
Now, I find out that you're just a stupid old guy...

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:01.340
...who makes trouble for other people.

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:03.940
It's so stupid and pitiful, I can't even cry or fart.

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:07.450
It's true, I'm the one who summoned Taizanfukun,

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:08.780
O Seimei-san, my butt!

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:09.880
...but its power was activated because you, Sasshi...

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:13.910
...wanted very badly to nullify someone's death!

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:15.520
Me?

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:17.450
Someone died?

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:21.700
Masa-jii...

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:23.390
So, that's it.

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:27.200
I never expected the fate linking Masayuki to me would curse you too.

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:29.030
That time, Masa-jii...

00:18:31.010 --> 00:18:34.770
No, Masa-jii got hooked and saved, I'm sure of it.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:40.750
The thing that fell was...

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:48.990
As long as you keep denying Masayuki's death...

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:51.560
...you won't be able to return to your own world.

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:54.070
Then, if we go back, Masa-jii will...

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:58.570
Most certainly be dead.

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:01.990
Mister...

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:05.840
No, Seimei-sama, isn't there, isn't there any good way?

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:06.790
No.

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:10.870
I won't call you a stupid mister anymore, so please forgive me!

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:13.610
Isn't there, isn't there any good way to solve this?!

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:13.840
No.

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:15.880
Scientifically speaking, there's none at all.

00:19:16.850 --> 00:19:18.450
Don't be so heartless!

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:20.380
This heartlessness is due to a logical conclusion!

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:45.380
So long, Pops!

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:47.410
Man, I'm so bored.

00:19:48.050 --> 00:19:51.040
Hey, I didn't notice before. My horn is gone.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:03.060
I suppose being able to cry is a child's prerogative.

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:06.010
How about becoming an Onmyou mystic?

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:08.840
Learn how the world works, gain lots of knowledge...

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:10.600
...stand at the pinnacle of scholarly achievements...

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:13.040
...and then you can decide for yourself.

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:16.870
Should you return to your original world? Or not?

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:21.110
Asahina Arumi's fate will also be in your hands.

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:23.950
Both Arumi and Masa-jii?

00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:26.120
I'm going to decide for them?

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:31.850
Mister, you said I've got potential, right?

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:34.420
Yeah, that's exactly why you're in this current situation.

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:37.630
All right! I'll study!

00:20:37.930 --> 00:20:41.200
I'll study harder than I've ever studied, become an Onmyou mystic...

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:43.930
...and take Arumi to the best possible world there is!

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:45.460
Good!

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:48.640
But Arumi's kinda impatient.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:52.180
I doubt she'd wait for me for 20 years...

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:55.480
You are the perpetrator!

00:20:55.950 --> 00:20:56.360
Number 2!

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:57.690
Namiko-san!

00:20:58.120 --> 00:21:00.710
The TV here doesn't have anything good on.

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:03.180
Oh, damn it!

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:06.590
Sasshi, you idiot!

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:22.730
Master, good morning.

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:27.550
Master, I had no idea you dressed like that too, my lord, Sir.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:29.650
I'll have to you know...

00:21:29.650 --> 00:21:32.450
...adults don't get to goof off all the time like you kids.

00:21:32.950 --> 00:21:34.270
I've got work to do.

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:36.810
I've got some goblins to banish.

00:21:37.760 --> 00:21:41.020
Since you're a goblin, go off somewhere and make a geekland or something.

00:21:41.260 --> 00:21:46.000
Hey! You said you'd teach me the science and techniques of the Onmyou Way!

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:47.160
I don't know!

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:50.080
Thinking about what you really are, it suddenly sounds absurd!

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:52.840
What I really am?

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:54.710
You mean, 'cause I'm a goblin?

00:21:55.740 --> 00:21:56.640
What's this?

00:21:56.640 --> 00:21:58.580
It's a trial kit for Onmyou mystic training.

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:00.880
Read the instructional materials in there and study.

00:22:01.180 --> 00:22:04.280
What's up with that?! That's like totally cutting corners!

00:22:04.280 --> 00:22:07.960
C'mon, Mister, teach me properly! C'mon, c'mon!

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:10.290
Who cares?! Just hurry up and get out of my sight!

00:23:46.390 --> 00:23:47.150
Next time on...

00:23:47.150 --> 00:23:48.200
You shut yer yap!

00:23:48.490 --> 00:23:50.760
Having spent some time being bored and with few appearances...

00:23:50.760 --> 00:23:53.060
...Arumi seizes the right to do the next episode preview from Sasshi.

00:23:53.330 --> 00:23:55.330
Does the Onmyou mystic training that Sasshi is about to embark on...

00:23:55.330 --> 00:23:57.630
...only exist in order to appease Arumi?

00:23:57.630 --> 00:23:59.400
Arumi, no fair! The preview is my...

00:23:59.400 --> 00:24:00.870
Sit still, why don't ya?!

00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:02.770
Arumi once again recovers the right to the preview...

00:24:02.770 --> 00:24:04.510
...and she finds herself in a new world.

00:24:04.510 --> 00:24:07.030
Its utter stupidity causes the girl to abandon all hope.

00:24:07.440 --> 00:24:10.070
Next time, "Fluffy, Bubbly, Abenobashi Fairy Tale Shopping Arcade!"

00:24:10.380 --> 00:24:13.080
All right, next time, it's going to be a circus! A circus!

00:24:13.080 --> 00:24:14.620
Uh, it ain't a circus.
